CLAIM: CUB lateroll@29 achieves 81.39% versus MaskedKD’s 80.22% on final seeds 1–3, a +1.17 pp difference [95% CI +0.75, +1.58], at 12.9900 versus 12.9881 GFLOPs/image; the gain is below the 1.92 pp promotion threshold.
VERDICT: NEEDS-MORE
REASON: The six cited runs support the numerical comparison, including final_lateroll_k29_s1_1101_104303_ef38 versus final_maskedkd_k29_s1_1101_104303_b676; historical locks MATCH. However, the bundle truncates before the actual outputs of analysis_cub_rollout_depth_1031_100143_a4b6 and analysis_cub_lateroll_decomp_1101_070348_b793. Supply those outputs and the missing H-C2b proposal entry to verify grounding, chronology and decomposition; researcher summaries cannot substitute.
The rollout caveat also needs correction: final improvement is +0.94, not +0.50 pp, still below threshold. The swap summary supports teacher-fidelity preservation, not causal attribution of student-accuracy gains. Novelty is weak: the source restricts existing [attention rollout](https://aclanthology.org/2020.acl-main.385/) to later layers.